Day 304/350: Can Partition Grid

Problem Statement #3548

Problem Statement Explantion:

Given a 2D grid of integers, determine if it is possible to partition the grid into two non-empty rectangular parts by a single vertical or horizontal cut such that:

The sums of the two parts are already equal.
OR, by moving exactly one element from one part to the other, the sums of the two parts become equal.
The move must be valid: the element moved from Part A must be added to the sum of Part B (and subtracted from Part A).

Solution Approach:

The core challenge is that a cut can be horizontal or vertical, and the "shiftable" element could be anywhere in the grid. We use two primary techniques to simplify this:

1. Geometric Symmetry (Rotations)
Instead of writing separate logic for horizontal and vertical cuts, we solve for horizontal cuts only and rotate the grid 90 degree four times. This covers:

Top-down cuts.
Bottom-up cuts.
Left-right cuts.
Right-left cuts.

2. The "Tag" Logic (Prefix Sums)
For any horizontal cut at row i, let:
S = Sum of all elements from row 0 to i.
T = Total sum of the entire grid.

Here's the Code:

class Solution {

    public boolean canPartitionGrid(int[][] grid) {
        long total = 0;
        int m = grid.length;
        int n = grid[0].length;
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                total += grid[i][j];
            }
        }
        for (int k = 0; k < 4; k++) {
            Set<Long> exist = new HashSet<>();
            exist.add(0L);
            long sum = 0;
            m = grid.length;
            n = grid[0].length;
            if (m < 2) {
                grid = rotation(grid);
                continue;
            }
            if (n == 1) {
                for (int i = 0; i < m - 1; i++) {
                    sum += grid[i][0];
                    long tag = sum * 2 - total;
                    if (tag == 0 || tag == grid[0][0] || tag == grid[i][0]) {
                        return true;
                    }
                }
                grid = rotation(grid);
                continue;
            }
            for (int i = 0; i < m - 1; i++) {
                for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                    exist.add((long) grid[i][j]);
                    sum += grid[i][j];
                }
                long tag = sum * 2 - total;
                if (i == 0) {
                    if (
                        tag == 0 || tag == grid[0][0] || tag == grid[0][n - 1]
                    ) {
                        return true;
                    }
                    continue;
                }
                if (exist.contains(tag)) {
                    return true;
                }
            }
            grid = rotation(grid);
        }
        return false;
    }

    public int[][] rotation(int[][] grid) {
        int m = grid.length;
        int n = grid[0].length;
        int[][] tmp = new int[n][m];
        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
                tmp[j][m - 1 - i] = grid[i][j];
            }
        }
        return tmp;
    }
}

Complexity:

Time Complexity:	O(M×N)
Space Complexity:	O(M×N)



